  "chunks": [
    {
      "chunk_type": "isnad",
      "arabic_text": "عَنْهُ عَنْ مُحَمَّدِ بْنِ الْوَلِيدِ وَ مُحَسِّنِ بْنِ أَحْمَدَ جَمِيعاً عَنْ يُونُسَ بْنِ يَعْقُوبَ قَالَ",
      "translations": {
        "en": "From him, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid and Muhsin ibn Ahmad, both, from Yunus ibn Ya'qub, who said:"
      }
    },
    {
      "chunk_type": "body",
      "arabic_text": "سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ عَلَيْهِ السَّلَامُ عَنِ الرَّجُلِ يُرِيدُ أَنْ يَتَزَوَّجَ الْمَرْأَةَ فَأَحَبَّ أَنْ يَنْظُرَ إِلَيْهَا قَالَ «تَحْتَجِرُ ثُمَّ لْتَقْعُدْ وَ لْيَدْخُلْ فَلْيَنْظُرْ» قَالَ قُلْتُ تَقُومُ حَتَّى يَنْظُرَ إِلَيْهَا قَالَ «نَعَمْ» قُلْتُ فَتَمْشِي بَيْنَ يَدَيْهِ قَالَ «مَا أُحِبُّ أَنْ تَفْعَلَ».",
      "translations": {
        "en": "I asked Abu Abdillah (peace be upon him) about a man who wants to marry a woman and wishes to look at her. He said: 'She stays in seclusion (hijr), then she sits, and he enters and looks at her.' I said: 'She stands up so that he looks at her?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'And she walks in front of him?' He said: 'I do not like her to do that.'"
      }
    }
  ],
  "translations": {
    "en": {
      "summary": "This hadith outlines the etiquette for a man viewing his prospective bride before marriage. The Imam instructs that the woman should remain in a secluded place (hijr) while the man enters and looks at her, rather than her standing or walking in front of him, which the Imam prefers less.",
      "seo_question": "What is the proper Islamic etiquette for a man to view his prospective bride before marriage?",
      "key_terms": {
        "أَبُو عَبْدِ اللَّهِ": "Abu Abdillah (Imam al-Sadiq, peace be upon him)",
        "يَتَزَوَّجَ": "to marry",
        "يَنْظُرَ": "to look/view",
        "تَحْتَجِرُ": "she stays in seclusion (hijr)",
        "بجر - a place of residence/seclusion for women in Islamic tradition)"
